<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!-- What to do about the moods of ailments and illnesses (Defs/ThoughtDefs/Council_Thoughts_Ailments.xml). -->

  <ColonyCouncil.MoodHintDef>
    <defName>Council_Mood_RF_AilColds</defName>
    <thoughts>
      <li>Council_Ail_HeadCold_Mood</li>
      <li>Council_Ail_ChestCold_Mood</li>
      <li>Council_Ail_LingeringCough_Mood</li>
    </thoughts>
    <fix>Bed rest, warmth and time. A cold passes in about a week and a chest cold in one or two. Keep the old and the frail warm and fed, so it doesn't turn into pneumonia.</fix>
    <article>Council_Alm_4_25_Ailments</article>
  </ColonyCouncil.MoodHintDef>

  <ColonyCouncil.MoodHintDef>
    <defName>Council_Mood_RF_AilStomachBug</defName>
    <thoughts><li>Council_Ail_StomachBug_Mood</li></thoughts>
    <fix>Rest and time; it's over in two or three days. Tending helps a little.</fix>
    <article>Council_Alm_4_25_Ailments</article>
  </ColonyCouncil.MoodHintDef>

  <ColonyCouncil.MoodHintDef>
    <defName>Council_Mood_RF_AilEyesAndPollen</defName>
    <thoughts>
      <li>Council_Ail_HayFever_Mood</li>
      <li>Council_Ail_Pinkeye_Mood</li>
    </thoughts>
    <fix>Have a doctor tend it; industrial medicine works best on both. Indoor work keeps hay fever down while the plants are in flower.</fix>
    <article>Council_Alm_4_25_Ailments</article>
  </ColonyCouncil.MoodHintDef>

  <ColonyCouncil.MoodHintDef>
    <defName>Council_Mood_RF_AilDreamfever</defName>
    <thoughts><li>Council_Ail_Dreamfever_Mood</li></thoughts>
    <fix>Rest and quiet. It passes in under a week.</fix>
    <article>Council_Alm_4_25_Ailments</article>
  </ColonyCouncil.MoodHintDef>

  <ColonyCouncil.MoodHintDef>
    <defName>Council_Mood_RF_AilStrains</defName>
    <thoughts>
      <li>Council_Ail_StrainedBack_Mood</li>
      <li>Council_Ail_SprainedAnkle_Mood</li>
      <li>Council_Ail_SoreHands_Mood</li>
    </thoughts>
    <fix>A day or two in bed at the start (or other work, for sore hands), then light work until it heals. Tending speeds it along.</fix>
    <article>Council_Alm_4_25_Ailments</article>
  </ColonyCouncil.MoodHintDef>

  <ColonyCouncil.MoodHintDef>
    <defName>Council_Mood_RF_AilSmallHurts</defName>
    <thoughts>
      <li>Council_Ail_Blisters_Mood</li>
      <li>Council_Ail_StiffNeck_Mood</li>
      <li>Council_Ail_Chilblains_Mood</li>
      <li>Council_Ail_Sunburn_Mood</li>
    </thoughts>
    <fix>It heals in a few days. A proper bed prevents a stiff neck, warm clothes chilblains, and a hat sunburn.</fix>
    <article>Council_Alm_4_25_Ailments</article>
  </ColonyCouncil.MoodHintDef>

  <ColonyCouncil.MoodHintDef>
    <defName>Council_Mood_RF_AilAir</defName>
    <thoughts>
      <li>Council_Ail_SmokeCough_Mood</li>
      <li>Council_Ail_EyeStrain_Mood</li>
      <li>Council_Ail_RimrotCough_Mood</li>
      <li>Council_Ail_AshLung_Mood</li>
    </thoughts>
    <fix>Better rooms: move a wood fire out of a small room, light the bench, and keep bedrooms clean, dry and roofed. Clean air clears the coughs; tending eases rimrot and ash lung.</fix>
    <article>Council_Alm_4_25_Ailments</article>
  </ColonyCouncil.MoodHintDef>

  <ColonyCouncil.MoodHintDef>
    <defName>Council_Mood_RF_AilToothache</defName>
    <thoughts><li>Council_Ail_Toothache_Mood</li></thoughts>
    <fix>One treatment from a doctor settles it within a day or two. Fewer sweets keep it from coming back.</fix>
    <article>Council_Alm_4_25_Ailments</article>
  </ColonyCouncil.MoodHintDef>

  <ColonyCouncil.MoodHintDef>
    <defName>Council_Mood_RF_AilConvalescent</defName>
    <thoughts><li>Council_Ail_Convalescent_Mood</li></thoughts>
    <fix>Rest, food and time. Time in bed shortens it.</fix>
    <article>Council_Alm_4_25_Ailments</article>
  </ColonyCouncil.MoodHintDef>

  <ColonyCouncil.MoodHintDef>
    <defName>Council_Mood_RF_AilSerious</defName>
    <thoughts>
      <li>Council_Ail_Tetanus_Mood</li>
      <li>Council_Ail_Pneumonia_Mood</li>
      <li>Council_Ail_Tuberculosis_Mood</li>
      <li>Council_Ail_Typhus_Mood</li>
      <li>Council_Ail_Meningitis_Mood</li>
      <li>Council_Ail_Glassblood_Mood</li>
      <li>Council_Ail_Cholera_Mood</li>
      <li>Council_Ail_HiveFever_Mood</li>
      <li>Council_Ail_Measles_Mood</li>
    </thoughts>
    <fix>Keep the patient in bed and tended as often as possible, with the best medicine the colony has. The illness's description says what helps most; for tuberculosis, every day without gaps, and for cholera, someone to keep them drinking.</fix>
    <article>Council_Alm_4_25_Ailments</article>
  </ColonyCouncil.MoodHintDef>

  <ColonyCouncil.MoodHintDef>
    <defName>Council_Mood_RF_AilScurvy</defName>
    <thoughts><li>Council_Ail_Scurvy_Mood</li></thoughts>
    <fix>Fruit or vegetables, raw or cooked into meals. Nothing else cures it, and it clears within about 10 days of eating them again.</fix>
    <article>Council_Alm_4_25_Ailments</article>
  </ColonyCouncil.MoodHintDef>

  <ColonyCouncil.MoodHintDef>
    <defName>Council_Mood_RF_AilDoctor</defName>
    <thoughts>
      <li>Council_Ail_HardCase</li>
      <li>Council_Ail_PulledThrough</li>
      <li>Council_Ail_Survived</li>
    </thoughts>
    <fix>It passes in two days. Good medicine on the shelf and a second doctor make a hard case lighter to carry.</fix>
    <keep>It comes from seeing someone through a serious illness.</keep>
    <article>Council_Alm_4_25_Ailments</article>
  </ColonyCouncil.MoodHintDef>

  <ColonyCouncil.MoodHintDef>
    <defName>Council_Mood_RF_AilAppendicitis</defName>
    <thoughts><li>Council_Ail_Appendicitis_Mood</li></thoughts>
    <fix>Have a doctor do the "remove appendix" operation (two medicine). Until then, tend the patient as often as possible.</fix>
    <article>Council_Alm_4_25_Ailments</article>
  </ColonyCouncil.MoodHintDef>

  <ColonyCouncil.MoodHintDef>
    <defName>Council_Mood_RF_AilRabies</defName>
    <thoughts><li>Council_Ail_Rabies_Mood</li></thoughts>
    <fix>Treat the bite every day, without a gap, until it's gone: treatment only works before the fever comes. Industrial medicine or better works fastest.</fix>
    <article>Council_Alm_4_25_Ailments</article>
  </ColonyCouncil.MoodHintDef>

  <ColonyCouncil.MoodHintDef>
    <defName>Council_Mood_RF_AilPainful</defName>
    <thoughts>
      <li>Council_Ail_KidneyStone_Mood</li>
      <li>Council_Ail_Shingles_Mood</li>
      <li>Council_Ail_NervePain_Mood</li>
    </thoughts>
    <fix>Neither can kill. Tending eases the pain and speeds it along; industrial medicine works best. A kidney stone passes within a week, shingles in two or three.</fix>
    <article>Council_Alm_4_25_Ailments</article>
  </ColonyCouncil.MoodHintDef>

  <ColonyCouncil.MoodHintDef>
    <defName>Council_Mood_RF_AilSleepAndHead</defName>
    <thoughts>
      <li>Council_Ail_Insomnia_Mood</li>
      <li>Council_Ail_Migraine_Mood</li>
    </thoughts>
    <fix>A dark, quiet room and a regular bedtime. Fewer late nights, regular meals and less to worry about keep them away; a doctor can help with either.</fix>
    <article>Council_Alm_4_25_Ailments</article>
  </ColonyCouncil.MoodHintDef>

  <ColonyCouncil.MoodHintDef>
    <defName>Council_Mood_RF_AilPassing</defName>
    <thoughts>
      <li>Council_Ail_Heartburn_Mood</li>
      <li>Council_Ail_Hiccups_Mood</li>
      <li>Council_Ail_MotionSick_Mood</li>
      <li>Council_Ail_Nosebleed_Mood</li>
      <li>Council_Ail_Splinter_Mood</li>
    </thoughts>
    <fix>They pass within hours. A doctor picks out a splinter in one go and eases travel sickness; smaller helpings stop heartburn.</fix>
    <article>Council_Alm_4_25_Ailments</article>
  </ColonyCouncil.MoodHintDef>

  <ColonyCouncil.MoodHintDef>
    <defName>Council_Mood_RF_AilSkin</defName>
    <thoughts>
      <li>Council_Ail_InsectBites_Mood</li>
      <li>Council_Ail_PlantRash_Mood</li>
      <li>Council_Ail_HeatRash_Mood</li>
      <li>Council_Ail_ColdSore_Mood</li>
      <li>Council_Ail_AthletesFoot_Mood</li>
      <li>Council_Ail_Frostnip_Mood</li>
    </thoughts>
    <fix>They heal in days, and a doctor's salve eases most of them. Long sleeves and nets in swamps and jungles, gloves in the fields, cooler bedrooms in the heat, dry socks, and mittens in the bitter cold prevent them.</fix>
    <article>Council_Alm_4_25_Ailments</article>
  </ColonyCouncil.MoodHintDef>

  <ColonyCouncil.MoodHintDef>
    <defName>Council_Mood_RF_AilLice</defName>
    <thoughts><li>Council_Ail_Lice_Mood</li></thoughts>
    <fix>Have a doctor treat them, then clean the room they sleep in: lice spread in dirty rooms, and they carry typhus.</fix>
    <article>Council_Alm_4_25_Ailments</article>
  </ColonyCouncil.MoodHintDef>

</Defs>
